      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-03T19:10:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I would have to dig into the NPCX implementation, but I\u0027m pretty sure that if there is an error in i2cxfer, it will leave the i2c in a good state. The i2c_read_string() that i mostly copied, only calls the i2c_lock() if the first transfer fails as well.",
