    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7a451325_acb46171",
        "filename": "board/eve/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-03T18:15:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are reads not allowed to be larger than block_len? If so, should we return error on (block_len !\u003d len)? The caller will expect that len bytes were read into buf on success return.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 405,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d77a09d957f56a7e125f1641a2b20a120f6ce812",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5bd60fb2_8addc55c",
        "filename": "board/eve/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1123814
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-03T19:10:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s my understanding that the battery will return how many bytes could be read from the block. So len could be less than block_len. This function is bascially a copy of i2c_read_string(), but here I truncate block_len to len instead of to len-1. I am fairly certain that the len-1 results in getting 1 too few bytes back.",
      "parentUuid": "7a451325_acb46171",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 405,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d77a09d957f56a7e125f1641a2b20a120f6ce812",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bdd943be_707aac2d",
        "filename": "board/eve/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-03T20:34:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "i2c_read_string() is tailored to the smart battery spec:\n\nstring a block of chars (32 byte maximum) where the first byte indicates the number of chars in\nthe block and is exclusive (e.g. {08,\u0027M\u0027,\u0027y\u0027,\u0027B\u0027,\u0027a\u0027,\u0027t\u0027,\u0027t\u0027,\u0027C\u0027,\u0027o\u0027} is a block containing nine chars, the first (08) is\nthe length of the string and the second through the ninth chars form the string, \"MyBattCo\")\n\nAre you sure reads to mfgacc work in the same way w.r.t. block length? It\u0027s suspicious because we\u0027re reading binary data here, not null terminated strings.\n\ncallers to i2c_read_string() just expect to get back a null terminated string, so it\u0027s reasonable to not read back all len characters, if the string isn\u0027t log enough. But this is a different case, if I call board_battery_read_mfgacc(..., 4), and the function returns success, there should be four read bytes in my buffer.",
      "parentUuid": "5bd60fb2_8addc55c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 405,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "d77a09d957f56a7e125f1641a2b20a120f6ce812",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f00c708d_f8ab8e47",
        "filename": "board/eve/battery.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 405,
      "author": {
        "id": 1001696
      },
      "writtenOn": "2017-10-03T21:02:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is a generic ManufacturerAccess routine I found:\n\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/#/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/409638/7/driver/battery/smart.c\n\nThe first byte read back does represent the size in bytes of subsequent data, including the two repeated cmd bytes.\n\nI still maintain that callers of board_battery_read_mfgacc() will expect `len` bytes to be read, if success status is returned.\n\nIt\u0027s probably fine for your use here, I just hope nobody reuses this code.",
      "parentUuid": "bdd943be_707aac2d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 403,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 405,
        "endChar": 18
      },
